{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: one glob matcher, one admin rule set, one snapshot commit (simplification review 55563589, findings DUP-02, LAYER-03, CRUFT-04, ARCH-02, ARCH-05, DUP-04, LAYER-05, LAYER-07). (1) room/src/glob.ts re-implements policy/src/glob.ts and has drifted: room refuses patterns over 256 characters and ** inside a segment; policy checks neither, so a policy can activate with a glob the Room would refuse in a claim, and one pattern goes through two matchers in one room. Move the stricter rules into policy, export overlapIsCertain and pathProblem there, delete room's copy. (2) room/src/obligations.ts:36-47 and admission.ts:495-503, 716-720, 732-743 copy policy/src/admin.ts and rules.ts (admin scope, self-review scopes, the recovery-scope refusal text, the admin obligation); import them from policy and let policy own the recovery-lane skips. (3) git/src/landing/core.ts:68-69 keeps ACTIVE and PRE_RESERVATION private, so the Room re-encodes the state classes at core.ts:575, 1251, admission.ts:1394, 1402 and jobs.ts:296; export isUnreserved, isReserved and retryFix from git. (4) The filtered-snapshot commit is derived in room/src/snapshot.ts:16-57 and checkers/src/snapshot-commit.ts:12-70 with separate tree encoders, and the author is declared a third time in git/src/publisher/gitops.ts:130; R-CARRY-15 requires identical IDs. One snapshotCommit in the package that owns git object encoding, with EMPTY_TREE, ZERO_SHA and gitObject exported once. (5) Rename same-name different-shape types (DiffResult, PreviewResult, PublisherPort, PushOutcome, TreeEntry, and the contract shadows Signer, ExecResult, Invitation, CheckerName) and import ActivePolicy and ActMeter from policy in the Room.","body":{"conditions":"room/src/glob.ts gone and room/test/node/glob.test.ts passing against policy; a test shows room and checkers compute the same snapshot commit ID from one function; no duplicated admin constants (grep test); no two exported types share a name across p